1. Understanding the context in which WFP operates
is core to protection, and critical to identifying and
addressing protection risks – and then jointly designing
programmes with affected populations. Placing people
at the centre of our decision-making, design and
consultation process will support stronger outcomes,
none of which is possible in the absence of working
collectively with other agencies in-country. Refer to
the following country office protection resources for
reporting on this section:
a. Protection Risk Assessment;
b. Protection Analysis;
c. Privacy Impact Assessments;
d. Assessments conducted by the Protection Cluster/
Sectors;
